# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EDA tool working directories (Cadence) — entirely generated, never committed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# genus  = synthesis, innovus = place & route, xcelium = simulation, .cadence = session state
genus/
# innovus/myshkin is frozen single-core PD output -- entirely generated, never committed.
# innovus/common (was innovus_mp/) holds hand-maintained tcl/sh/Makefile source PLUS a
# large amount of generated + PDK-derived P&R output (dbs/ out/ log/ rpt/ work/
# timingReports/, qrc/voltus logs, timing files, via-viol reports, netlists...). Like the
# old blanket `innovus/` rule and innovus/myshkin/, both trees are ignored wholesale; the
# hand-maintained source (Makefile, prep_top_netlist*.sh, tcl/, in/chip_top.*) is already
# tracked and stays tracked -- add any NEW source file with `git add -f`.
innovus/myshkin/
innovus/common/
.cadence/
# Pegasus/Calibre DRC-LVS run logs:
ic_bad/
# logo/ contained *.gds:
logo/
# NOTE: xcelium/ is intentionally NOT blanket-ignored. It is handled by the
#       "XCELIUM SIMULATION SOURCES" whitelist at the bottom of this file, which
#       tracks run scripts / test lists / testbenches and drops all sim artifacts.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FOUNDRY / PDK IP — NEVER commit. TSMC (and any foundry) PDK data is under NDA.
# Layout, timing, netlist, and tech files embed foundry-proprietary information.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.gds
*.gds2
*.oas
*.lef
*.def
*.def.gz
*.sdf
*.spef
*.cdl
*.oa
*.lvs.v
*.route.gz
# any file whose name carries the foundry/PDK name:
*tsmc*

# Generic EDA/simulation intermediates (in case tools run elsewhere)
*.rcf
*.trn
*.dsn
*.pak
*.svcf
*.diag
INCA_libs/
xcelium.d/
*.shm/
.simvision/
xrun.log
xrun.history
xrun.key

