# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# XCELIUM SIMULATION SOURCES  (default-deny whitelist — keep setup, drop artifacts)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Goal: version only the human-authored simulation setup (run scripts, test/cell
# lists, testbench sources) — NEVER the multi-GB generated artifacts (compiled
# libs, waveforms, logs, snapshots). Kept at the bottom so it is evaluated last.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore has NO inline comments — every '#' must start its own line.
#
# 1) Ignore everything under xcelium/ by default:
xcelium/**
# 2) but descend into every subdirectory so files below can be re-included:
!xcelium/**/
# 3) re-include only these source / setup file types
#    (run scripts, control scripts, testbenches, file/test/cell lists):
!xcelium/**/*.sh
!xcelium/**/*.tcl
!xcelium/**/*.do
!xcelium/**/*.vhd
!xcelium/**/*.sv
!xcelium/**/*.svh
!xcelium/**/*.v
!xcelium/**/*.vh
!xcelium/**/*.f
!xcelium/**/*.txt
!xcelium/**/*.md
!xcelium/**/README*
!xcelium/**/Makefile
# 4) …but ALWAYS drop these, even if they matched a rule above (last word wins).
#    Artifact dirs: compiled libs/snapshots, waveforms, SimVision state,
#    symbol caches, logs, local AI settings, generated RAM images.
xcelium/**/xcelium.d/
xcelium/**/waves.shm/
xcelium/**/.simvision/
xcelium/**/.bpad/
xcelium/**/log/
xcelium/**/.claude/
xcelium/**/ram_images/
xcelium/**/*.svcf
xcelium/**/xrun.key
xcelium/**/xrun.log
xcelium/**/xrun.history
# make verify staging flows (generated by platform/common/verify.sh --
# fully regenerable, incl. their .sh/.txt/.vhd, so exempt from the whitelist):
xcelium/riscv_test/verify_*/
# Generated data dumps that happen to be .txt (edit if you actually want them):
xcelium/**/sig_approx_fp.txt
xcelium/**/output_results.txt
xcelium/**/*_actual_*.txt

# Local engineering changelog (not for the repo)
.devlog/

# Publications / conference materials copied in for local reference (not for the repo)
docs/publications/

# The interactive roadmap + block-diagram pages (docs/vestarv_roadmap.html,
# docs/castalia_soc.html, docs/vestarv_core.html, docs/castalia_full.html) are
# PUBLISHED since the 2026-07-16 showcase program (GitHub Pages, D1).

# Myshkin AFE bidirectional-current design note (local, not for the repo for now)
implementations/asic/myshkin-2025-11/docs/afe-bidirectional-current-upgrade.html

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# S4b showcase hygiene (2026-07-16) — additive untracked-noise suppression.
# Kept at the very bottom so the xcelium-scoped rules below WIN over the
# XCELIUM SIMULATION SOURCES whitelist above (last matching pattern wins).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Syncthing conflict copies (broader than the *.sync-conflict-* rule above —
# also catches variants without the trailing dash / leading dot):
*sync-conflict*

# Root Innovus / Pegasus session logs dropped in the repo root:
/innovus.cmd
/innovus.log*
/pegasus_ui_gui.log

# signoff_mp: generated foundry OA cell libs, tool stdout dumps, dated backups:
signoff_mp/chip_top_signoff/
signoff_mp/chip_argus_signoff/
signoff_mp/pvs/*.stdout
*.jul*.bak

# M19c one-shot debug tooling — stays on disk (user decision) but stops showing
# as untracked noise. These live inside xcelium/, where *.tcl/*.sh are
# whitelisted above, so they must be re-ignored here (after the whitelist):
xcelium/riscv_test/behavioral_mp/m19c_probe*.tcl
xcelium/riscv_test/innovus_mp/diag_*.sh

